1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,944
When you lose weight, the fat doesn't melt
away or turn into muscle,

2
00:00:03,944 --> 00:00:05,767
and you don't sweat it out either,

3
00:00:05,767 --> 00:00:09,143
because most of it leaves your body every
time you breathe out.

4
00:00:09,593 --> 00:00:12,781
And when scientists asked 150 doctors,

5
00:00:12,781 --> 00:00:17,800
dietitians and personal trainers where the
fat goes, only three of them got it right.

6
00:00:18,250 --> 00:00:23,164
Because fat is made of just three kinds of
atoms, carbon, hydrogen and oxygen,

7
00:00:23,164 --> 00:00:25,179
and when your body needs energy,

8
00:00:25,179 --> 00:00:28,644
it breaks the fat apart with the oxygen
you breathe in.

9
00:00:29,094 --> 00:00:33,539
Then the pieces join up again as carbon
dioxide, the gas you breathe out,

10
00:00:33,539 --> 00:00:38,653
and as water, which leaves in your sweat,
your tears, your pee and even your breath.

11
00:00:39,103 --> 00:00:44,587
So if you lose 10 kg of fat, 8.4 kg of it
leave through your lungs,

12
00:00:44,587 --> 00:00:47,423
and only 1.6 kg turn into water.

13
00:00:47,873 --> 00:00:49,783
But breathing faster won't help,

14
00:00:49,783 --> 00:00:54,798
because your body only burns more fat when
it needs more energy, like when you move,

15
00:00:54,798 --> 00:00:57,425
and panting on purpose just makes you
dizzy.

16
00:00:57,875 --> 00:01:00,126
So even right now, as you watch this,

17
00:01:00,126 --> 00:01:03,533
a tiny bit of you is leaving every time
you breathe out.
